  "construction": {
    "inputs": "A sealed validated F128FixedTableV0 Shannon program and explicit compilation limits only; no arbitrary layers, guest, point, expected value, statement, proof, native verifier witness, SRS or key.",
    "exactness": "At each layer, reachable source cofactors decode into a GF(2) basis. Elimination acts on exact pairs of child coefficient vectors, retaining residual basis rows and source decoders. Leaves span the 128-bit constants; skipped coordinates have identical cofactors. Evaluating low + x * (low XOR high) uses each coordinate once, preserving all Boolean-cube coefficients and hence the F128 multilinear polynomial. Davio input is refused rather than expanded.",
    "proof_status": "Algebraic construction with exhaustive small-coefficient tests, native differentials and materialized R1CS negatives; not a new kernel-certified refinement theorem or a full-relation soundness proof.",
    "ownership": "Immutable fields/read-only getters; no unchecked constructor. The approved root compiler derives structure from its own exact diagram and propagates every budget failure without fallback.",
    "adopted_programs": {
      "binary_linear_matrices": 2,
      "decision_diagram_matrices": 44,
      "cofactor_basis_structure": 1,
      "decision_diagram_jagged": 1
    },
    "adoption": "Only structure changes representation, following the paired exact constraint measurement. Successful rank compilation alone does not authorize adopting other candidate tables.",
    "smaller_limits": {
      "state_slots": 4000000,
      "dense_words": 16000000,
      "word_operations": 200000000,
      "coefficient_terms": 8000000
    },
    "limit_scope": "Per basis compiler. Dense words are cumulative u64 payload allocations including scratch, not peak resident memory, and exclude the source DAG and container/allocator overhead. Source diagrams separately use the unchanged global 64000000-entry/2000000-node limit. Logical budgets are not whole-pipeline proving admission."
  },
